.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
.TH LUNDUKE-TERMINAL 1 "2026-11-12" "Lunduke Terminal @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lunduke-terminal \- retro CRT-style terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lunduke-terminal
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.RB [ \-e | \-x
.IR COMMAND " [" ARG ]...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lunduke-terminal
is a GTK 3 terminal emulator with optional CRT effects.
It is the default terminal on LCOS 1.1.0.
The package provides the Debian
.B x-terminal-emulator
alternative and an XFCE preferred-application helper, so a panel launcher,
Thunar's "Open Terminal Here" and
.B exo-open \-\-launch TerminalEmulator
can all start it.
.PP
.B lunduke-terminal \-\-help
lists every option and key.
The options below are the ones
.B x-terminal-emulator
callers, Thunar and exo pass.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e " " \fICOMMAND\fR " [" \fIARG\fR ...]
Run
.I COMMAND
instead of the user's shell.
Everything after
.B \-e
is the command and its arguments.
Those arguments are passed to
.BR execvp (3)
and are not interpreted by a shell.
This option must be last.
.TP
.BR \-x " " \fICOMMAND\fR " [" \fIARG\fR ...]
.PD 0
.TP
.BR \-\-execute " " \fICOMMAND\fR " [" \fIARG\fR ...]
.PD
Same as
.BR \-e .
XFCE's helper runs
.B %B \-x %s
, which is this form.
.TP
.BR \-T " " \fITITLE\fR
.PD 0
.TP
.BR \-\-title " " \fITITLE\fR
.PD 0
.TP
.BR \-\-title= \fITITLE\fR
.PD
Set the window title.
.TP
.BR \-\-cwd " " \fIDIR\fR
.PD 0
.TP
.BR \-\-workdir " " \fIDIR\fR
.PD 0
.TP
.BR \-\-working-directory " " \fIDIR\fR
.PD
Working directory of the shell or
.IR COMMAND .
.BR \-\-cwd= \fIDIR\fR,
.BR \-\-workdir= \fIDIR\fR
and
.BR \-\-working-directory= \fIDIR\fR
are accepted as well.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the full help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print
.B lunduke-terminal @VERSION@
and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/org.lunduke.LundukeTerminal.desktop
Menu and panel launcher
.RB ( Categories=System;TerminalEmulator; ).
.TP
.I /usr/share/xfce4/helpers/lunduke-terminal.desktop
XFCE preferred-application helper
.RB ( "X-XFCE-Category=TerminalEmulator" ).
Select it with
.B TerminalEmulator=lunduke-terminal
in
.IR ~/.config/xfce4/helpers.rc .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lunduke-terminal/settings.ini
Saved settings. Command-line options override it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR x-terminal-emulator (1)
